description:
FILED s539a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-13).

Reproducer (scratch/s539a/pr2/ts1.pl):
  use Test::More tests => 3;
  ok(1, "first");
  TODO: { local $TODO = "not yet"; todo_skip "cannot run", 1; }
  ok(1, "last");
perl: `not ok 2 # TODO & SKIP cannot run` then `ok 3 - last`, exit 0.  PCL (main 24988e35): `Undefined subroutine &main::todo_skip called`, exit 255 after row 1.  Test::More's todo_skip(WHY, COUNT) emits COUNT `not ok N # TODO & SKIP WHY` rows and `last TODO`; Test::Builder->todo_skip(WHY) emits one.  ->details reports such a row as { ok => 1, actual_ok => 0, type => 'todo_skip', reason => WHY, name => '' }.  The row record s539a added (`%test-record-row`) already has the shape; the function is the missing part.  Fix in cl/pcl-test.lisp (Test::More export + Test::Builder method); guard in Pl/t/tap-assert-01.t.

=== DONE (s539a) ===
Test::More's todo_skip(WHY, COUNT): COUNT `not ok N # TODO & SKIP WHY` rows (no COUNT: one, with Test::More's "needs to know $how_many" warning unless no_plan), then `last TODO`; Test::Builder->todo_skip(WHY) one row; ->details type todo_skip (ok 1, actual_ok 0).  pl-todo_skip is exported from :pcl (the eager TAP export list) and in *tap-api*.  Guard Pl/t/tap-assert-01.t row 45 (fails on the base).  The warning's location reads `at unknown line 0.` (#233 / #4790).
